a":"அவன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொண்ட","parts":[{"text":"கொண்ட","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"held"}],"gloss":"held"},{"surface":"குடுமித்தும்","parts":[{"text":"குடுமித்து","lemma":"குடுமி","gloss":"having a peak"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"under control also"},{"surface":"இத்","parts":[{"text":"இத்","lemma":"இத்","gloss":"this"}],"gloss":"this","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தண்பணை","parts":[{"text":"தண்","lemma":"தண்","gloss":"cool"},{"text":"பணை","lemma":"பணை","gloss":"fertile field"}],"gloss":"cool fertile land"},{"surface":"நாடே","parts":[{"text":"நாடு","lemma":"நாடு","gloss":"country"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"country indeed"}]}],"literal":"Of the kinfolk cooking vessel to be filled, long banner / non-blooming Vañci also he will give, is it only that? / Cosmetics smeared, curved joints, bamboo-like shoulders, / bright forehead female dancers, 'may they receive the price of flowers', saying, / mansion-filled Madurai also he will give, all. / Let us sing, come, gift-seeking people! / Ancient land ownership if considered, good wisdom / potter children potter's wheel placed / wet clay bright lump like, his / held peak-like control also, this cool fertile country indeed.","translation":"To fill the cooking vessels of our kinfolk, he will give Vañci of the long banners, which does not bloom. Is that all? Saying, 'Let the bright-foreheaded female dancers with bamboo-like shoulders and curved joints smeared with cosmetics receive the price of flowers,' he will also give Madurai of the tall mansions. Come, O seekers of gifts, let us sing of him! If we consider his ancient right over this land, this cool, fertile country is under his control, easily shaped like a bright lump of wet clay placed on a wheel by a potter's children.","modern":"நம் சுற்றத்தாரின் சமையல் பாத்திரங்கள் நிறையும்படி, நீண்ட கொடிகளைக் கொண்ட, பூக்காத வஞ்சி மாநகரையும் அவன் தருவான். அதுமட்டும் அல்லாமல், நறுமணப் பூச்சு பூசிய, வளைந்த முன்கைகளையும் மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களையும் ஒளிபொருந்திய நெற்றியையும் உடைய விறலியர் பூ வாங்குவதற்கான விலையைப் பெறட்டும் என்று கூறி, மாட மாளிகைகள் நிறைந்த மதுரை மாநகரையும் அவன் பரிசாகத் தருவான். பரிசில் பெறும் மக்களே, வாருங்கள்! நாம் அவனைப் பாடுவோம். அவனது அறிவுத்திறனையும் இந்தத் தொன்மையான நிலத்தின் மீதான அவனது உரிமையையும் ஆராய்ந்து பார்த்தால், குயவனின் சிறுவர்கள் சக்கரத்தில் வைத்த பசிய களிமண்ணின் திரண்ட உருண்டை போல, இந்தத் குளிர்ந்த வயல்சூழ்ந்த நாடு முழுவதும் அவனது ஆளுகைக்கு உட்பட்டு அவன் விருப்பப்படி வளையும் தன்மையுடையதாக இருக்கிறது.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Paṭāṇ tiṇai (praising a king's greatness) and the Iyaṉmoḻi tuṟai (describing the king's natural qualities). The poet Kōvūr Kiḻār is addressing other bards and artists, urging them to join him in singing the praises of the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi. He highlights the king's extraordinary generosity, stating that Nalaṅkiḷḷi would readily give away the Cera capital Vañci just to fill the cooking pots of his poets' relatives, and the Pandya capital Madurai just to buy flowers for the female dancers. The poet uses a striking simile of a potter's children shaping a lump of wet clay on a wheel to describe how easily the entire fertile land of the Tamil country yields to the king's wise and ancient right of rule. Key words include 'வஞ்சி' (Vañci), 'மதுரை' (Madurai), 'பரிசில் மாக்கள்' (seekers of gifts), and 'பசுமண் குரூஉத்திரள்' (bright lump of wet clay).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,1.7],[1.7,2.2],[2.2,3.1],[3.1,3.3],[3.3,3.6],[3.6,4.0],[4.0,4.8],[4.8,5.0],[5.0,5.8],[5.8,6.1],[6.36,7.4],[7.4,7.8],[7.8,8.0],[8.0,8.7],[8.7,8.9],[8.9,9.5],[9.5,9.8],[9.8,10.1],[10.1,10.5],[10.5,11.7],[11.7,12.3],[12.3,12.3],[12.3,13.2],[13.2,13.9],[14.0,14.5],[14.5,14.7],[14.7,14.9],[14.9,16.1],[16.1,16.5],[16.5,16.7],[16.7,17.1],[18.08,18.78],[18.78,19.08],[19.18,19.58],[19.58,19.88],[19.88,20.28],[20.28,20.78],[20.83,20.93],[20.93,21.08],[21.08,21.46]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,2.0],[2.0,2.7],[2.7,3.5],[3.5,3.7],[3.7,4.1],[4.1,4.6],[4.6,5.7],[5.7,5.9],[5.9,6.7],[6.7,7.0],[7.0,8.2],[8.2,8.2],[8.2,8.8],[8.8,9.4],[9.4,9.7],[9.7,10.4],[10.4,10.7],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,11.4],[11.4,12.8],[12.8,13.4],[13.4,13.5],[13.5,14.3],[14.3,14.83],[14.9,15.4],[15.4,15.6],[15.6,15.9],[15.9,16.83],[16.99,17.3],[17.3,18.4],[18.4,18.5],[19.6,20.3],[20.3,20.72],[20.8,21.2],[21.2,21.6],[21.6,22.0],[22.0,22.6],[22.6,22.95],[22.95,23.3],[23.3,23.6]]},"sync":[[["கடும்பின்","of the kinfolk"]],[["அடுகலம்","cooking vessel"]],[["நிறையாக","so as to be filled"]],[["நெடுங்","long"]],[["கொடிப்","banner"]],[["பூவா","non-blooming"]],[["வஞ்சியும்","Vañci also"]],[["தருகுவன்","he will give"]],[["ஒன்றோ","is it only that?"]],[["வண்ணம்","cosmetics"]],[["நீவிய","smeared"]],[["வணங்குஇறைப்","curved joints"]],[["பணைத்தோள்","bamboo-like shoulders"]],[["ஒண்ணுதல்","bright forehead"]],[["விறலியர்","female dancers"]],[["பூவிலை","price of flowers"]],[["பெறுக","may they receive"]],[["என","saying"]],[["மாட","mansion-filled"]],[["மதுரையும்","Madurai also"]],[["தருகுவன்","he will give"]],[["எல்லாம்","all"]],[["பாடுகம்","let us sing"]],[["வம்மினோ","come!"]],[["பரிசில்","gift-seeking"]],[["மாக்கள்","people"]],[["தொன்னிலக்","ancient land"]],[["கிழமை","ownership"]],[["சுட்டின்","if considered"]],[["நன்மதி","good wisdom"]],[["வேட்கோச்","potter"]],[["சிறாஅர்","children"]],[["தேர்க்கால்","potter's wheel"]],[["வைத்த","placed"]],[["பசுமண்","wet clay"]],[["குரூஉத்திரள்","bright lump"]],[["போல","like"]],[["அவன்","his"]],[["கொண்ட","held"]],[["குடுமித்தும்","under control also"]],[["இத்","this"]],[["தண்பணை","cool fertile land"]],[["நாடே","country indeed"]]]}